<id/18/1831/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Manna"@en ;
    skos:broadMatch <customs-1866/sap/#concept> ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_drugs_medicinal_botanicals/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "a sweet gummy exudation from several plants: the Calabrian manna is produced in tears from a species of ash, the *Fraxinus rotundifolia*, while some is obtained from another species, the *F. florifera*. The oriental manna of the desert is from *Alhagi Maurorum*. Manna is used medicinally. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 251]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated fields — source_taxon remove: 'Oriental manna' aside; commercial manna is Fraxinus ornus."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "1831" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Manna"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Historical materia medica heading: sweet medicinal exudate from manna ash (Fraxinus ornus) imported from Italy and Spain."@en ;
